                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c092f7e-73fc-4365-a6b1-0568176f294e",
                                                "sense_id": "3ac79d65-149b-3423-89e2-196f5714ae30",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: cask"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1415ad73-8222-41ed-a040-7c5546727a72",
                                                "sense_id": "3ac79d65-149b-3423-89e2-196f5714ae30",
                                                "text": "a cracker barrel"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8973c8c4-875f-4aaa-aa43-12ea5b213b16",
                                                "sense_id": "3ac79d65-149b-3423-89e2-196f5714ae30",
                                                "text": "The dawn of the oil age was fairly recent. Although the stuff was used to waterproof boats in the Middle East 6,000 years ago, extracting it in earnest began only in 1859 after an oil strike in Pennsylvania. The first barrels of crude fetched $18 (around $450 at today’s prices)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "831c6aeb-339a-3874-88fe-aa6e8e83e183",
                                        "entry_id": "59d1479b-4f20-3b39-9505-b60619b50f99",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A round (cylindrical) vessel, such as a cask, of greater length than breadth, and bulging in the middle, made of staves bound with hoops, and having flat ends (heads). The word is sometimes applied to a similar cylindrical container made of metal, usually called a drum.",
                                            "Such a cask of a certain size, holding one-eighth of what a tun holds. (See a diagram comparing cask sizes.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b58a7567-831e-403a-a111-4c23c18ee0a0",
                                                "sense_id": "831c6aeb-339a-3874-88fe-aa6e8e83e183",
                                                "text": "Barrels came in firkins, nine gallons; kilderkins, eighteen gallons; halves, twenty-seven gallons; barrels, thirty-six gallons and hogsheads, fifty-four."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c22c748-bb9c-3e34-afe2-5a67aae06cb6",
                                        "entry_id": "59d1479b-4f20-3b39-9505-b60619b50f99",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quantity which constitutes a full barrel: the volume or weight this represents varies by local law and custom."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f3e093b-88b2-44bb-9f17-89cf773f9ecb",
                                                "sense_id": "2c22c748-bb9c-3e34-afe2-5a67aae06cb6",
                                                "text": "Again, by 28 Hen. VIII, cap. 14, it is re-enacted that the tun of wine should contain 252 gallons, a butt of Malmsey 126 gallons, a pipe 126 gallons, a tercian or puncheon 84 gallons, a hogshead 63 gallons, a tierce 41 gallons, a barrel 31.5 gallons, a rundlet 18.5 gallons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9c911a7-e8c8-4dfb-9774-ca44067c0437",
                                                "sense_id": "2c22c748-bb9c-3e34-afe2-5a67aae06cb6",
                                                "text": "23 Hen. VIII, cap. 4... The barrel of beer is to hold 36 gallons, the kilderkin 18 gallons the firkin 9. But the barrel, kilderkin, and firkin of ale are to contain 32, 16, and 8 gallons."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa5f5dac-f180-3edc-a944-e04fa30e9d49",
                                        "entry_id": "59d1479b-4f20-3b39-9505-b60619b50f99",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A solid drum, or a hollow cylinder or case"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94e436df-479b-4178-aa04-4776af32f286",
                                                "sense_id": "fa5f5dac-f180-3edc-a944-e04fa30e9d49",
                                                "text": "the barrel of a windlass; the barrel of a watch, within which the spring is coiled."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "35721c01-7992-3d34-acbc-9e0eb3142ca6",
                                        "entry_id": "59d1479b-4f20-3b39-9505-b60619b50f99",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A metallic tube, as of a gun, from which a projectile is discharged."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cdf027b4-8ca6-43c4-b8c0-a98a790ad72c",
                                                "sense_id": "35721c01-7992-3d34-acbc-9e0eb3142ca6",
                                                "text": "You're shooting stars from the barrel of your eyes"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "941d59f5-daaf-3da8-9b1c-97084ee194dd",
                                        "entry_id": "59d1479b-4f20-3b39-9505-b60619b50f99",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A venturi (in carburetion)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c784422-6467-350b-b75a-e7f601ad705a",
                                        "entry_id": "59d1479b-4f20-3b39-9505-b60619b50f99",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ceiling-mounted tube from which lights are suspended."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e02f132-ff95-4d68-8355-53d22c97c36f",
                                                "sense_id": "1c784422-6467-350b-b75a-e7f601ad705a",
                                                "text": "Moreover, it adds to difficulties in adjusting/servicing lamps located over high scenery, ceilings etc., where the barrel networks cannot be lowered or reached."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a7444ba-e4a6-4f84-aefb-6ec76ee992a6",
                                                "sense_id": "1c784422-6467-350b-b75a-e7f601ad705a",
                                                "text": "The barrel, which is usually from 2.0 m to 2.5 m long, and capable of lifting loads up to 120 kg, is suspended from the main housing which contains the motor gearbox unit, etc."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
